            <ArticleTitle>Tubercular infection in the sacrococcygeal pilonidal sinus--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>648-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1742-481X.2008.00518.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of multiple pus discharging sinuses in the sacrococcygeal region in a 22-year-old man, who had a history of episodes of pain and pus discharge since 8 months. The patient underwent radiofrequency sinotomy using a Ellman radiofrequency device and was treated with antitubercular treatment, which resulted in complete resolution, and healing of the wound.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
